      "content": "Ibuprofen can help manage the pain and inflammation, but antibiotic ointment alone might not be enough for a significant burn. Applying a thin layer of an over-the-counter antibiotic ointment *after* thoroughly cooling the burn is acceptable for minor burns, but you must monitor it closely. If the redness continues to spread significantly or if the pain becomes unbearable, you need to seek professional medical advice to ensure it heals correctly and prevent complications.",
